[001] 
[002]  ▀▀█  v1.4.0
[003]  █╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
[004]  P│ Projects · Repo > feat-pi-shared-context-ux-07-feedback                                     │
[005]   │  [1 Tracker]     2 Files    Tab focus · Space/Enter activate                                │
[006]  P│ Initiatives  >  Improve shared-con…  >  pi-shared-context-…  >  Description                 │
[007]   │> Select shared-context projects through interactive breadcrumbs · Description               │
[008]   │                                                                                             │
[009] [C│  ## What to build                                                                           │
[010]   │                                                                                             │
[011]   │  Add the Projects view to the shared-context modal. Users open this view through a          │
[012] [E│  focusable, clickable Projects breadcrumb. Users select a project and browse its existing   │
[013]   │  tracker and Files workspace.                                                               │
[014]   │                                                                                             │
[015] [E│  Reuse shared-context enumeration and route resolution. Include the current project.        │
[016]   │  Deduplicate entries by canonical identity. Do not scan unrelated repositories or add       │
[017] /r│  another project registry.                                                                  │edb
[018] ac│                                                                                             │
[019]   │  Establish the breadcrumb and focus contract for later tracker screens. The current command │
[020] tu│  still opens the current project. Selecting another project changes only the modal context. │
[021] /r│                                                                                             │edb
[022] ac│  ## Acceptance criteria                                                                     │
[023] /r│                                                                                             │edb
[024] ac│  1. The project list displays a name and origin or stable identity for each project. Equal  │
[025]   │  repository names remain distinguishable.                                                   │
[026]   │  2. Keyboard focus reaches the Projects breadcrumb. Enter activates it. A mouse click       │
[027]  W│  activates the same control.                                                                │
[028]   │  3. Selecting a project resolves its routes before record access. The selected project owns │
[029]  /│  tracker reads, Files reads, and action targets.                                            │ee
[030]  d│  4. The header displays Shared or Repo from the selected alignment route. The indicator is  │en
[031]  d│  read-only.                                                                                 │
[032]   │  5. Project selection does not change the active Pi session directory or system             │
[033]  /│  instructions.                                                                              │ee
[034]  d│  6. Returning to a project restores its navigation, selection, and scroll position. Each    │en
[035]  d│  workspace retains independent state.                                                       │
[036]   │  7. Project changes dispose of old watchers and attach the correct new watchers. Old        │
[037]   │  project updates do not change the selected project view.                                   │
[038]   │  8. A project without a usable checkout retains readable context. Checkout-dependent        │
[039]   │  actions display a clear disabled reason.                                                   │
[040]   │                                                                                             │
[041] ──│ [Return]  [PgUp] [PgDn]                                                                     │───
[042]   │↑↓ scroll · PgUp/Dn page · Esc return                                                        │
[043] ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
